update modules set pip_name = $t$plr-ivoryos[usb]==1.0.0b2$t$, module_name = $t$STAR$t$, module_path = $t$plr_ivoryos.hamilton$t$, init_args = $j$[{"name": "simulated", "type": "bool", "default": true}, {"name": "deck_type", "type": "str", "default": "STARLetDeck"}, {"name": "worktable", "type": "str", "default": "worktable.json"}, {"name": "device_address", "type": "int"}, {"name": "serial_number", "type": "str"}, {"name": "step_delay_s", "type": "float", "default": 0}]$j$::jsonb, schema = (select s->$t$STAR$t$ from _schemas), schema_source = 'introspection', updated_at = now(), description = $t$A Hamilton STAR, STARlet or STARplus (deck_type STARDeck, STARLetDeck or STARPlusDeck) through PyLabRobot 1.0. The robot is one instrument and each thing fitted to it another (star_pipettes, star_head96 or star_head384, star_iswap, star_core_grippers, star_autoload), each with PyLabRobot's own steps. Simulated (the default) is PyLabRobot's own STAR simulator, answering as the firmware would; for the real one on USB, untick simulated. Beta: pinned to PyLabRobot 1.0.0b1, run in simulation only. Decks on one computer share one Python environment, so this replaces the PyLabRobot that any older plr-ivoryos driver there needs. Add the Labware plugin after this driver to see and edit the worktable.$t$ where id = 178;

