update modules set pip_name = $t$plr-ivoryos[usb]==1.0.0b2$t$, module_name = $t$EVO$t$, module_path = $t$plr_ivoryos.legacy$t$, init_args = $j$[{"name": "simulated", "type": "bool", "default": true}, {"name": "deck_type", "type": "str", "default": "EVO150Deck"}, {"name": "worktable", "type": "str", "default": "worktable.json"}, {"name": "diti_count", "type": "int", "default": 0}, {"name": "channels", "type": "int", "default": 8}, {"name": "step_delay_s", "type": "float", "default": 0}]$j$::jsonb, schema = (select s->$t$EVO$t$ from _schemas), schema_source = 'introspection', updated_at = now(), description = $t$A Tecan Freedom EVO 100, 150 or 200 (deck_type EVO100Deck, EVO150Deck or EVO200Deck) through PyLabRobot. PyLabRobot 1.0 drives this robot only through pylabrobot.legacy, so it is one instrument with every LiquidHandler operation (pick_up_tips, aspirate, dispense, move_plate, ...), PyLabRobot's names and arguments; wells are written as PyLabRobot writes them (assay_plate[A1:H1]). Simulated (the default) is PyLabRobot's legacy chatterbox: its tip and volume tracking, not the robot's firmware. Beta: pinned to PyLabRobot 1.0.0b1, run in simulation only. PyLabRobot 1.0.0b1 cannot make a Tecan tip rack yet, so the worktable has no disposable tips. For the real one on USB, untick simulated. Decks on one computer share one Python environment, so this replaces the PyLabRobot that any older plr-ivoryos driver there needs. Add the Labware plugin after this driver to see and edit the worktable.$t$ where id = 186;

